{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Class Based Programming", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about programming.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Talk about particular topics related to sofware programming.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "OOP", "type": "name"}, {"content": "object oriented programming; a programming language model organized around objects and not mathematical logic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Class-based programming is a style of OOP where the classes of objects are the ones that give inheritance to other objects. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "CBP", "type": "name"}, {"content": "class-based programming; a style of OOP that divides the objects into classes according to their characteristics", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Class-based programming is a style of OOP where the classes of objects are the ones that give inheritance to other objects. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "break", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to interrupt the regularity from a class in CBP", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It prevents the users from breaking the invariants of a class.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "parent class", "type": "name"}, {"content": "main class from CBP that can define new subclasses according to specific characteristics from the main class", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The first class is the parent class.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "style", "type": "name"}, {"content": "set of rules used to write a source code for a computer program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This style of programming classifies each object in a class according to its features.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Past Continuous and Simple Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <b>past continuous</b> and <b>simple past</b> to talk about things that happened in the past and finished in the past too.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<b>Past Continuou</b> s<br/> <br/> Use <b>past continuous</b> when you want to talk about something that was in progress at a specific time in the past. With this tense, you provide a more extended context to a story or situation. <br/> Follow this structure for affirmative statements: <br/> <br/> <div class=\"center_text\">subject + be in past (<b>was</b>/ <b>were</b>) + main verb with <b>ing </b>+ complement</div><br/> <br/> Example: <br/> They <b>were programming</b> when the boss called for a meeting. <br/> <br/> <b>Simple Past</b><br/> <br/> You can use <b>simple past</b> to talk about actions that started and finished at specific moments in the past. <br/> <br/> This is the structure you use to make affirmative sentences: <br/> <br/> <div class=\"center_text\">subject + <b>main verb in past</b>+ complement</div><br/> <br/> Example: <br/> We <b>worked</b> for 3 months on that program.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Why weren't you in class today? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "First, we learned that Class-based programming is a style of OOP where the classes of objects are the ones that give inheritance to other objects. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I thought we were studying that topic next week.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Specific pronouns with verbs in singular: Either, Each, and Nothing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Use <strong>each</strong>, <strong>either</strong> or <strong>nothing</strong> to compare two things and talk about specific objects.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Use <strong>either</strong> to express alternatives or a choice between two things.</li></ul></br>  Example:</br><i> I can use <strong>either</strong> prototype based <strong>or</strong> class-based programming for this project.</i></br></br>  <ul><li>Use <strong>each</strong> to talk about different factors or parts of a whole as individuals.</li></ul></br>  Example:</br><i> <strong>Each</strong> object can have different classes.</br></br></i>  <ul><li>Use <strong>nothing</strong> as an indefinite pronoun to show the absence of a thing in affirmative sentences.</li></ul></br>  Example:</br><i> There was <strong>nothing</strong> to do about the programming language they chose.</i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This style of programming classifies each object in a class according to its features. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I need more clarification on each feature ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can organize classes either in tree, if it is single inheritance, or in lattice, if it's multiple inheritance.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Programming and computer science terms ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are certain terms you need to understand from programming and computer science.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Fat Binary:</strong> It is a computer executable program that is possible to run in multiple processor types because it is expanded with a native code. </br>  <strong>Filename Extension:</strong> It is the suffix you give to a computer file. This indicates the characteristics of the file and the programs that can run it.</br>  <strong>First Generation Programming Language:</strong> This language is a grouping of programming languages you use to program first generation computers. The instructions made in 1GL (First Generation Programming Language) were in binary numbers.</br>  <strong>FTP Client:</strong> It is a software service that allows the connection between a remote server and a host computer. It permits a dual direction transfer of data and files.</br>  <strong>Functional Programming:</strong> It is a style used to build the structure and elements of a computer program. It is a declarative programming paradigm; for this reason, you use it with declarations and expressions instead of statements.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for expanded information on classes and objects in OOP. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a brief presentation to your class in which you explain the importance of classes and objects within the languages that support OOP. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Provide your classmates and instructor with new and relevant information about these concepts.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I look for expanded information on classes and objects in OOP. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a brief presentation about the importance of classes and objects. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I provide my classmates and instructor with new and relevant information about these concepts.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can explain the concept of class based programming.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can give detailed information about class based programming.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify important features related to class based programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What types of Object Oriented Programming (OOP) styles do you know?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Have you used any OOP style? Which one?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's learn something about Class-Based programming.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "type": "WLC"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], 